    <!-- Help Screen Strings -->
    <string name="help_title">Frequently Asked Questions</string>
    <string name="help_dashboard_title">1. Dashboard &amp; Statistics</string>
    <string name="help_dashboard_desc">The Dashboard provides an overview of your driven distances and worked hours. Use \'Week\', \'Month\' and \'Year\' to adjust the period. Statistics are shown for your preferred vehicle by default. You can filter manually per vehicle via the car icon. The location icon in the top bar shows the tracking status: green is active, blue is ready to go, and gray means permissions are missing. The dashboard also shows a private usage warning bar if this is configured for the active vehicle.</string>
    <string name="help_bluetooth_title">2. Automatic Trip Registration</string>
    <string name="help_bluetooth_desc">CIMDriver runs in the background. As soon as your phone connects to the Bluetooth carkit of your vehicle, the trip starts automatically. When the connection is lost, the app first waits for the configured grace period. If the connection does not return, the trip is finished and presented for review.\n\nYou can adjust this grace period via the menu: Settings → Tracking.</string>
    <string name="help_manual_title">3. Add Trips Manually</string>
    <string name="help_manual_desc">Did you use a different car, or was Bluetooth turned off? You can always add a trip manually. The app pre-selects your default vehicle. If you enter the \'New odometer\', the app calculates the distance. If you leave it empty, the app calculates the route based on the entered addresses.</string>
    <string name="help_merge_title">4. Review &amp; Merge Trips</string>
    <string name="help_merge_desc">New automatic trips get the status \'To review\'. In the overview, you can directly choose Commute, Business or Private. Via \'More options\' you choose a specific Dynamics trip type. Tap the trip for details or to merge trips. You can easily delete a trip by swiping it to the left.\n\nNote: If the driven distance deviates more than 10% (and at least 2 km) from the expected shortest route, you will be prompted to enter a mandatory explanatory note during the review.</string>
    <string name="help_classification_title">5. Business, Private or Commute?</string>
    <string name="help_classification_desc">The category and Dynamics trip type of a trip are automatically determined by your classification rules. A rule links two address types, for example \'Home\' and \'Work\'. If the locations of your trip match this, the app automatically applies the configured category (Business, Commute, Private) and Dynamics trip type.\n\nRules are bi-directional by definition. This means they always work in both directions. A rule between \'Home\' and \'Work\' thus automatically recognizes the outbound trip (Home to Work) as well as the return trip (Work to Home). So you only need to create one rule for a round trip. If no rule matches, the trip keeps the status \'To review\'.\n\nYou can add, change and manage your own rules via the main menu under: Settings → Trip Classification.</string>
    <string name="help_hours_title">6. Hours Registration</string>
    <string name="help_hours_desc">Upon arrival at the work location, the work day starts. Upon returning home, it is presented for review. If the measured arrival or departure falls within the configured tolerance of your work hours, the app uses the configured times for the net calculation. Break time is only subtracted after more than 4 hours plus the configured tolerance.\n\nVia the filter button at the top (Week/Month) you can select the desired period directly from the dropdown. Use the search button to search by text, and delete hours by swiping left.\n\nConfigure your work hours, breaks and tolerance via the menu: Settings → Work Hours.</string>
    <string name="help_addressbook_title">7. Address Book &amp; Project Codes</string>
    <string name="help_addressbook_desc">Save frequently visited addresses in the Address Book. Check if it is a Client location to instantly register as Business. Tap the navigation icon (triangle) next to an address to start routing in your navigation app immediately.\n\nYou can also import addresses in bulk via the download icon at the top right. Select a CSV file with the following columns (including header):\nName,Description,Street,City\n\nNeed to find an address quickly? Use the search button at the top. You can easily delete an address by swiping it to the left.</string>
    <string name="help_vehicles_title">8. Manage Vehicles</string>
    <string name="help_vehicles_desc">Via \'Vehicles\' you add vehicles with license plate and starting odometer. You can also configure per vehicle if and when you want to receive a private usage warning. Tap the star icon next to a vehicle to set it as default.\n\nVia the \'Correct\' button in the edit screen you can enter a deviating odometer. You can choose how the app resolves any gap in the kilometers (e.g. distribute proportionally over previous trips). Delete a vehicle? Simply swipe the card to the left.</string>
    <string name="help_export_title">9. Export (CSV &amp; PDF)</string>
    <string name="help_export_desc">In Trips and Work Hours you can export detailed data as CSV or PDF. The Dynamics trip types are preserved in the detail export.</string>
    <string name="help_settings_title">10. Settings &amp; Permissions</string>
    <string name="help_settings_desc">In Settings you manage work hours, break and tolerance for net hours. You also manage classification rules, retention period of GPS points, backups and required permissions for Location, Bluetooth, Notifications and battery usage.</string>
    <string name="help_android_auto_title">11. Android Auto</string>
    <string name="help_android_auto_desc">Connect your phone to your car to activate Android Auto. You can stop your active trip, view and review recent trips, choose Dynamics trip types and navigate to addresses. Android Auto uses the same classification rules as the main app.</string>
    <string name="help_backup_title">12. Backup, Restore &amp; Privacy</string>
    <string name="help_backup_desc">A backup contains the full database, including trips, addresses, work hours, settings and classification rules. After a restore, an older database is automatically migrated to the current version. Android permissions are not included and must be granted again. GPS points are cleaned up according to the configured retention period.</string>
